---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
import SectionHeader from "../components/SectionHeader.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="ADHD Planner | Syntheion Dynamics"
  description="Visual planning tool with node canvas, image embeds, and timeline workflow."
  mode="canvas"
  sector="Planner"
  ogImage="/images/mini-planner-canvas.jpg"
>
  <Hero
    title="ADHD Planner"
    subtitle="Custom node-based planning canvas made to replace friction-heavy workflows."
    image="/images/mini-planner-canvas.jpg"
  />

  <section class="section container">
    <SectionHeader sector="Why" title="Why I built it" />
    <p>
      I tried to adapt to Obsidian for planning, but it did not fit the way I think. That friction pushed me to build
      my own visual planner. The prototype worked, then quickly became a real tool I use.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section container grid-2">
    <div>
      <SectionHeader sector="Features" title="Current feature set" />
      <ul>
        <li>Node canvas with effectively unlimited instances</li>
        <li>Image embedding and mixed visual/text planning</li>
        <li>Color-coded structure for fast context switching</li>
        <li>Timeline lane for sequencing and scheduling</li>
        <li>Scene and tooltip driven workflow details</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="muted">Status: personal production tool, release scope to be defined.</p>
    </div>
    <img class="enlargeable" src="/images/mini-planner-overview.jpg" alt="ADHD planner overview workspace" />
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
